#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD1023 expect=violation domain=LB
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=2 USUBJID=01-701-1015 VISIT="WEEK 99"
#note "JOINLESS BASELINE. RENAMED 2026-09-18 (review round 3) from 'violation_no_sv_dataset': that name asserted a premise FDA-SD1023 CANNOT have. The rule has NO Match_Datasets at all under D-TA-6a - grep -c Match_Datasets rules-src/checks/FDA/FDA-SD1023.yaml -> 0 - so there is no absent-joined-dataset path to enter and this fixture cannot guard one. It was originally kept (f0b866d4) as the in-tree record of the measurement that CORRECTED the plan: while the rule briefly carried a left SV join (phase 3, aca322b9), a study with no SV dataset was measured to KEEP the pre-join verdicts - the engine FOLDS the absent joined dataset rather than SKIPping the rule, against the plan's AbsentDatasetSkip prediction. That premise now lives in documentation/findings-snapshot-rebaselines.md, because no joinless fixture can assert it and a filename must not claim otherwise. What this fixture DOES pin, and why it is still here: the verdicts the rule has always had with no SV in sight - row 2 (WEEK 99, 99) is neutral-named and not a TV pair -> fires; row 1 (BASELINE, 2) is a TV pair -> clean. ⚠ Its data and expectations are byte-identical to FDA-SD1023-invalid-LB.cdt, so it is a DUPLICATE scenario kept only for that record; delete it knowingly, not by accident."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset LB label="Laboratory Test Results"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col LBSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col LBTESTCD type=Char label="Lab Test or Examination Short Name"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
col VISIT    type=Char label="Visit Name"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | 1 | ALB | 2  | BASELINE
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | 2 | ALB | 99 | WEEK 99
---

dataset TV label="Trial Visits"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
col VISIT    type=Char label="Visit Name"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | TV | 1 | SCREENING
CDISCPILOT01 | TV | 2 | BASELINE
---
